claims.canonical_value:
Given that $A(m,4)$ and $B(2,n)$ are on the graph of the inverse proportion function $y=\frac{4}{x}$,
\[
\begin{cases}
4=\frac{4}{m} \\
n=\frac{4}{2}
\end{cases}
\Rightarrow
\begin{cases}
m=1 \\
n=2
\end{cases}
\]
Thus $A(1,4)$ and $B(2,2)$.

Substituting $A(1,4)$ and $B(2,2)$ into $y=kx+b$, we get:
\[
\begin{cases}
4=k+b \\
2=2k+b
\end{cases}
\]
Solving gives:
\[
\begin{cases}
k=-2 \\
b=6
\end{cases}
\]
Therefore, the equation of the linear function is $y=-2x+6$.

